<title>USA: Italy to buy $116 million in U.S. missiles.</title>
<headline>Italy to buy $116 million in U.S. missiles.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defence Department informed Congress on Tuesday that Italy intends to purchase 233 U.S.-made AMRAAM air-to-air missiles for its AV-8B Harrier military jets.</p>
<p>Italy would pay an estimated $116 million for the package of AIM-120B advanced medium-range air-to-air missiles, made by Hughes Missile Systems Co. and Raytheon Co, the Pentagon said.</p>
<p>The department said Italy would use the missiles, which can be fired at enemy aircraft from over the horizon, to upgrade the air-to-air fighting capability of its Harriers.</p>
</text>
